"num_turns": 5, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "I found 11 rules whose behavior didn't match their docstrings and fixed all of them in `pricebook.py`. After the fix, all 150 rules give the same result as a reference built from the docstrings.\n\n| Type | Rules | Before → after |\n|---|---|---|\n| Discount was rounded, but the module docstring says to round down to the won | 02, 45, 86 | `round(base * p / 100)` → `base * p // 100` |\n| A \"whole\" rule only discounted units above the threshold | 28, 125 | `(qty - T) * unit * p // 100` → `base * p // 100` |\n| Discount didn't start at the threshold quantity itself | 15, 116, 130 | `qty > T` → `qty >= T` |\n| Discount started one unit late | 30, 139, 99 | `qty >= T+1` → `qty >= T` |\n\n**How I checked:** I read the type (whole/marginal), percentage, threshold and cap from each rule's docstring and built a reference for every rule from the module docstring's common rules. I then compared each rule to it for quantities 0–259 and 12 unit prices from 1 to 99,999. Before the fix, exactly these 11 rules differed. After the fix, none did.\n\nRule 92 (marginal, 30+ units) uses `qty >= 31` in its code. At 30 units a marginal discount is 0 either way, so prices don't change, and I left it alone. Changing it to `>= 30` would make the code clearer.\n\nSTATUS: DONE", "ttft_ms": 2421, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 31099, "uuid": "de4221e3-d90a-4f50-b0da-7b18dc0fd4d5", "ttft_stream_ms": 1715, "time_to_request_ms": 221, "time_to_request_phases_ms": {"other": 8, "system_prompt": 24, "resume_other": 10, "process_user_input": 1, "input_attachments": 4, "input_hooks": 1, "transcript_persist": 2, "tool_pool_refresh": 1, "init_message": 3, "engine_pickup": 1, "message_prep": 0, "model_config_wait": 1, "autocompact": 0, "query_setup": 0, "model_gates": 148, "tool_schema_build": 10, "message_normalization": 1, "client_creation": 3, "request_build": 3}, "turn_start_resume_kind": "none", "process_turn_index": 0, "t